Date:   Thu Nov 12 22:17:36 2026 +0000

    Scrub case variants, semicolon-separated and encoded keys in logged URIs
    
    The _scrub_uri helper matched query keys case-sensitively and split the query only on "&". Case variants of the listed keys, a token behind a semicolon separator, and a percent-encoded key all kept their values on the way to the logs. Keys are now decoded and lowercased before matching, extra keys are lowercased to match, the query splits on both separators, and password joins the default scrub list.

